  "layers": {
    "2eaa0d3f-2028-5c5a-9dad-49dcc01b6590": {"name":"OpenStreetMap","parameters":{"opacity":1.0,"source":"a3cc2d0f-d8de-5e16-ac50-fb885d432d1d"},"type":"RasterLayer","visible":true},
    "611b3c0c-aa15-53f2-a1bb-b62f7a29eeeb": {"name":"Ekurhuleni informal settlements (live municipal polygons)","parameters":{"color":{"fill-color":"#d95f0e","stroke-color":"#7f2704","stroke-width":1.5,"circle-fill-color":"#d95f0e","circle-radius":4.0,"circle-stroke-color":"#7f2704","circle-stroke-width":1.0},"opacity":0.78,"source":"531166a1-be6d-561a-83ab-b83cb5a49ff7","symbologyState":{}},"type":"VectorLayer","visible":true},
    "5640ca3a-65fa-532c-800e-efb5e0bfed84": {"name":"Informal settlements in Ekurhuleni","parameters":{"content":{"contentMode":"map","image":"","markdown":"This live layer comes from the **City of Ekurhuleni Metropolitan Municipality** and is explicitly published as **Informal Settlements** polygon data.  \n\nThe map is not a synthetic illustration: the orange outlines are fetched from the municipality's ArcGIS service when the story opens.  \n\nUse the **Identify** tool and click a polygon to inspect available attributes, including settlement name, households (2016 field), hectares, ward, classification, water, sanitation, lighting, and NUSP category.  \n\n**Important:** settlement status and boundaries can change. Treat the municipal layer as a dated administrative source, preserve its provenance, and do not infer informality from imagery alone.","title":"Informal settlements in Ekurhuleni"},"extent":[3128513.9253090248,-3051958.212503971,3172233.694282733,-2989425.3633173583],"layerOverride":[],"transition":{"time":1.4,"type":"smooth"},"zoom":3.2},"type":"StorySegmentLayer","visible":true},
    "974664f2-6c0a-54c3-a1bd-342eaa9ff249": {"name":"Northern Ekurhuleni — Thembisa area","parameters":{"content":{"contentMode":"map","image":"","markdown":"This chapter moves to **northern Ekurhuleni around Thembisa**. The highlighted municipal polygons remain the authoritative mapped objects in this example; the chapter extent is simply a geographic view into that live layer.  \n\nClick individual polygons to read their settlement-level attributes. This pattern can be repeated country-by-country: one authoritative polygon source, normalized metadata, then narrative chapters built from the geometries.","title":"Northern Ekurhuleni — Thembisa area"},"extent":[3132174.24855218,-3006682.629099771,3152211.756894969,-2990582.0662662494],"layerOverride":[],"transition":{"time":1.4,"type":"smooth"},"zoom":11.4},"type":"StorySegmentLayer","visible":true},
    "777bd727-6806-5c46-b86c-bd98b76317b4": {"name":"Eastern Ekurhuleni — Benoni area","parameters":{"content":{"contentMode":"map","image":"","markdown":"The eastern view demonstrates how a story map can move across a metropolitan inventory without duplicating the source data. The polygons are still read directly from the same municipal GeoJSON query.  \n\nFor the global repository, source adapters can download or normalize comparable polygon inventories and derive **representative latitude/longitude** and **bounding boxes** for each feature.","title":"Eastern Ekurhuleni — Benoni area"},"extent":[3141522.8593889987,-3031130.1791675705,3163786.7575476537,-3013762.6141648563],"layerOverride":[],"transition":{"time":1.4,"type":"smooth"},"zoom":11.2},"type":"StorySegmentLayer","visible":true},
    "5fb1d343-2599-5fed-8ab8-8cdb13c411c0": {"name":"Western Ekurhuleni — Germiston area","parameters":{"content":{"contentMode":"map","image":"","markdown":"In western Ekurhuleni, use the Identify tool to compare the service and classification fields attached to mapped settlement polygons.  \n\nA global story should keep these local attributes rather than flattening every source into a single universal definition. The canonical schema therefore retains source-specific classification, date, license, and provenance alongside geometry.","title":"Western Ekurhuleni — Germiston area"},"extent":[3125478.381180964,-3037503.112881031,3147742.279339619,-3018887.5973157827],"layerOverride":[],"transition":{"time":1.4,"type":"smooth"},"zoom":11.2},"type":"StorySegmentLayer","visible":true},
    "d9962804-8d99-5b66-85b7-3209bc42de9e": {"name":"Southern Ekurhuleni — Katlehong area","parameters":{"content":{"contentMode":"map","image":"","markdown":"The southern chapter shows the same live polygon inventory around **Katlehong and southern Ekurhuleni**.  \n\nThis is the intended presentation model for the repository: a reader can step through places, zoom to mapped informal-settlement polygons, inspect evidence, and then move outward to country and global comparisons.","title":"Southern Ekurhuleni — Katlehong area"},"extent":[3124036.793775191,-3054549.970312675,3146300.691933846,-3035912.4088608027],"layerOverride":[],"transition":{"time":1.4,"type":"smooth"},"zoom":11.2},"type":"StorySegmentLayer","visible":true},
    "9b1c99ce-cb59-5256-a4a8-49aa98cb105a": {"name":"From one city to a global atlas","parameters":{"content":{"contentMode":"map","image":"","markdown":"This Ekurhuleni story is the **live proof-of-concept**. The rest of the repository supplies the pipeline for scaling the pattern globally.  \n\nEach normalized settlement record can carry: polygon or multipolygon geometry; representative latitude/longitude; bounding box; source organization; source URL; observation date; license; classification; confidence/quality notes; and country ISO code.  \n\nOpen the notebooks in this repository to add additional authoritative datasets and generate country-specific `.jGIS` stories.","title":"From one city to a global atlas"},"extent":[3128513.9253090248,-3051958.212503971,3172233.694282733,-2989425.3633173583],"layerOverride":[],"transition":{"time":1.4,"type":"smooth"},"zoom":3.2},"type":"StorySegmentLayer","visible":true}
  },
